&lt;p&gt;At Lyft, our purpose is to serve and connect. We aim to achieve this by cultivating a work environment where all team members belong and have the opportunity to thrive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Data is at the heart of Lyft Business&#39;s products and decision-making. We&#39;re looking to hire a Data Analyst to build the tools and analytics that drive revenue for the sales organization behind Lyft&#39;s B2B portfolio — a multi-billion-dollar book of business spanning healthcare, business travel, corporate commute, automotive, and transit. This team has real say in what gets built.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be the analytical partner to our Sales and account teams — someone who can translate findings into a clear narrative for both technical and non-technical audiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the tools and analytics sales leaders use to grow their accounts — pacing views, account-health signals, territory and segment views that change what a rep or manager does next&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Field requests from Sales, Product, Finance, Legal, leadership, and external stakeholders, and decide what&#39;s worth building, what&#39;s worth a sharp piece of analysis, and what&#39;s out of scope&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain production data pipelines, and automate recurring workflows, with documentation and validation clear enough that a teammate — or an AI agent — can use them without asking you first&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define what the team&#39;s core metrics mean and where they live, so every dashboard, report, and tool returns the same answer to the same question&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the internal tools and semantic layer — prompts, context, and guardrails — that let stakeholders query B2B data in natural language and trust what comes back&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate insights into a cohesive narrative and present technical findings to senior leadership and non-technical audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree (or related work experience) with a focus in analytics, statistics, economics, computer science, or other quantitative fields&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in a data analytics or business intelligence role, ideally supporting a sales, go-to-market, or B2B organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in SQL — able to read, write, and review structured, efficient queries on large data sets, whether you wrote them yourself or an AI coding assistant did; you own the correctness of every query and result before it reaches stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building production data assets — pipelines, data models, or orchestrated tables (Airflow, dbt, or similar) — not only ad-hoc analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in a data visualization tool like Tableau, Hex, Mode, or similar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with sales or account analytics — pipeline, bookings, pacing to target, account segmentation — is a strong plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Python for data analysis and automation is a strong plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial instinct paired with a builder&#39;s instinct — a track record of turning a recurring request into a durable tool or dataset instead of answering it one more time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of influencing business decisions through analysis, and an ownership mindset toward the metrics and datasets you build&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills with the ability to tackle ambiguous problems, break them down, and deliver clear, actionable insights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills, with the ability to present complex data to a variety of stakeholders clearly and compellingly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong attention to detail and a commitment to data accuracy and integrity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to collaborate across functions, manage competing priorities, and drive projects to completion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Benefits:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Great medical, dental, and vision insurance options with additional programs available when enrolled&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family building benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Child care and pet benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) plan with company match to help save for your future&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In addition to 12 observed holidays, salaried team members have discretionary paid time off, hourly team members have 15 days paid time off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;18 weeks of paid parental leave. Biological, adoptive, and foster parents are all eligible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subsidized commuter benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly Lyft credits and complimentary Lyft Pink membership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
