&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced degree (MS or PhD, PhD preferred) in a quantitative field like Operations Research, Applied Math, Computer Science, Statistics, Engineering, or a related area; or equivalent work experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for solving unstructured and non-standard mathematical problems, with 2+ years of hands-on experience in optimization (preferred), causal inference, or machine learning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;End-to-end experience with data, including querying, aggregation, analysis, and visualization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with Python.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ability to collaborate and communicate with others in a team setting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience seeking out and adopting new methods and techniques.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing, running, and analyzing A/B tests to validate hypotheses and inform decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
