&lt;p&gt;Sitting within the broader Safety &amp;amp; Customer Care team, Lyft&#39;s Customer Care Operations organization manages over 1.7 million monthly customer interactions and serves as the company&#39;s primary direct touchpoint with riders, drivers, and businesses — spanning frontline support across multiple customer segments, a global BPO workforce, and the central functions that enable them to operate at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Director of Business Planning &amp;amp; Central Operations is a newly created role at the center of how Customer Care runs and grows. This leader will ensure the org is resourced and positioned for the future, and will own the functions that keep Customer Care financially disciplined and execution-ready. Reporting to the Senior Director of Customer Care Operations, they will lead five functions: Planning &amp;amp; Forecasting, Workforce Management, Readiness &amp;amp; Integration, Vendor Management, and Support Excellence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Business Planning &amp;amp; Strategy&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Senior Director to drive H1 and H2 planning — translating annual objectives into operational plans, investment decisions, and resource models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the investment brief process: sizing opportunities, articulating trade-offs, and building the business cases that secure resourcing for strategic priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
