&lt;p&gt;This role combines political campaign and project management leadership with political giving strategy and PAC management. You will serve as both a political strategist and operational manager, representing policy goals to internal and external stakeholders while supporting Lyft&#39;s comprehensive political engagement infrastructure. To support our Federal, State &amp;amp; Local Policy teams, you will lead the development and implementation of political campaigns—including legislative advocacy and state ballot initiatives; while simultaneously driving our political giving strategy and managing all PAC operations in support of the company&#39;s policy mission. Reporting to the Director of Campaigns, this role serves as an essential support function for the broader Policy team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Campaign Development &amp;amp; Management&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In partnership with our Director of Campaigns, design and implement strategic campaigns leveraging tactics such as rider and driver activation and engagement; earned, owned, and paid media; and leveraging, creating, and supporting coalitions and third party partners.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop campaign plans with clear goals, timelines, budgets, and messaging.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional collaboration across Policy, Communications, Legal, Product, Marketing teams and other internal partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Lyft on industry policy coalitions, building third-party support as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee campaign execution, ensuring adherence to timelines and budgets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a thought leader on political strategies, messaging, and tactics across the company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Political Giving Strategy &amp;amp; PAC Operations&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and drive Lyft&#39;s short-term and long-term political contribution strategy in partnership with the Chief Policy Officer and Policy Leadership Team, ensuring alignment with business priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set vision and strategy for Lyft&#39;s Federal PAC and State PACs, including internal growth targets and fundraising initiatives to maximize participation and contribution levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify high-impact opportunities to expand Lyft&#39;s political footprint and deepen relationships with elected officials and organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as subject matter expert on political giving strategy, providing regular briefings, impact analysis, and strategic recommendations to leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure comprehensive compliance with campaign finance law across federal, state, and local jurisdictions; manage external counsel relationships and establish robust compliance processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead quarterly state and local political giving cycles, including planning, budgeting, approvals, execution, and tracking across all Government Relations teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
